      "content": "\"Stopping the fight\" means accepting that the bright, perfect image you were curating was never truly real, and that's okay. You are not a stain; you are a human being who has made a mistake, and mistakes are messy, not permanent. If you can't preserve the past, perhaps you can choose to let the present moment be the quiet place where you finally give yourself permission to just *be* without the performance. You deserve to be seen as you are right now, even if that version is broken.",
